{"name":"Biker","title":"Biker","revision":231553,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Biker","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Bikers are a subculture revolving around riding motorcycles, and the lifestyle/culture associated with it. The biker aesthetic is not quite the bike itself, or anyone who rides one, but a specific type of style and attitude that is associated with it. The biker aesthetic is an image of toughness, roughness, sex appeal, and danger."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Origin"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Though motorcycles have been around since the 1800s (commercially, since the 1900s), 'biker culture' as we know it now has its roots in post-WWII. With the men coming back from service, motorcycle advertising changed to reflect a masculine aesthetic, with women being pushed out of the picture, or included only as passengers for sex appeal. This push was part of the post-war movement for men to return to their prior 'masculine' roles, with women returning to their 'housewife' duties."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Region"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Although the reach of the aesthetic has spread across the world, it's mainly associated with America, Australia, New Zealand, Japan, and Britain. The aesthetics vary by region, though all share common aesthetics, such as the tough and ‘criminal’ association."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather jackets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jacket patches (usually 'edgy' in nature)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tattoos"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bandanas"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bike helmets"},{"kind":"list","text":"jeans/ripped jeans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather vests"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beards"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fingerless gloves"},{"kind":"list","text":"DuRags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Carbon fibre"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kevlar nylon clothing"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Biker fashion changes culturally, but most incorporate leather, blacks and reds, studs, chains, jeans/denim, 'punk' styles, and 'edgy' styles. For women, there is usually an emphasis on sex appeal, while men emphasize masculinity and intimidation."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Movies"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Wild One (1953)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Wild Angels (1966)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hells Angels on Wheels (1967)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Easy Rider (1969)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Run, Angel, Run! (1969)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Losers (1970)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mad Max (1979)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Exterminators of the Year 3000 (1983)"},{"kind":"list","text":"City Limits (1985)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cobra (1986)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Akira (1988)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black Rain (1989)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nam Angels (1989)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harley Davidson and the Marlboro Man (1991)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stone Cold (1991)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Motorcycle Diaries (2004)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wild Hogs (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hell Ride (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Teen Beach Movie (2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Teen Beach 2 (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mad Max: Fury Road (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sons of Anarchy The Movie (2022)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sons of Anarchy (2008-2014)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mayans M.C. (2018-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"American Chopper (2003-2010, 2018-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Biker Build-Off (2002-2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ride with Norman Reedus (2016-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Biker Battleground Phoenix (2014)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Miami Ink\" (2005-2008)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ride to Hell: Retribution (2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Grand Theft Auto IV: The Lost And Damned (2009)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hell's Angels: A Strange and Terrible Saga by Hunter S. Thompson"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Metal, hard rock, and punk music is usually associated with bikers."},{"kind":"list","text":"AC/DC - Hell's Bells"},{"kind":"list","text":"AC/DC - Highway to Hell"},{"kind":"list","text":"Aerosmith - Sweet Emotion"},{"kind":"list","text":"Allman Brothers Band - Midnight Rider"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bon Jovi - Wanted Dead or Alive"},{"kind":"list","text":"CAKE - The Distance"},{"kind":"list","text":"Christopher Cross - Ride Like the Wind"},{"kind":"list","text":"Danzig - She Rides"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doobie Brothers - Rockin' Down the Highway"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doobie Brothers - China Grove"},{"kind":"list","text":"Motley Crue - Wild Side"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nazareth - Hair Of The Dog"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pantera - I'm Broken"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pantera - Cowboys from Hell"},{"kind":"list","text":"Foo Fighter - Wheels"},{"kind":"list","text":"George Thorogood and the Destroyers - Bad to the Bone"},{"kind":"list","text":"Joan Jett - Bad Reputation"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kid Rock - Born Free"},{"kind":"list","text":"Limp Bizkit - Rollin'"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lynyrd Skynyrd - Free Bird"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lynyrd Skynyrd - Sweet Home Alabama"},{"kind":"list","text":"Meat Loaf - Bat Out of Hell"},{"kind":"list","text":"Molly Hatchet - One Last Ride"},{"kind":"list","text":"Motörhead - Ace of Spades"},{"kind":"list","text":"Motörhead - You Better Run"},{"kind":"list","text":"Motörhead - Life's A Bitch"},{"kind":"list","text":"REO Speedwagon - Ridin' the Storm Out"},{"kind":"list","text":"Robert Earl Keen - The Road Goes On Forever"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sammy Hagar - I Can't Drive 55"},{"kind":"list","text":"Saxon - Motorcycle Man"},{"kind":"list","text":"Saxon - Wheels of Steel"},{"kind":"list","text":"Steppenwolf - Born to be Wild"},{"kind":"list","text":"Thin Lizzy - Whiskey in the Jar"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tom Petty - Runnin' Down a Dream"},{"kind":"list","text":"Willie Nelson - On the Road Again"},{"kind":"list","text":"ZZ Top - La Grange"},{"kind":"list","text":"Zeke - Death Alley"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Motorcycles and Motorcycle Cultures\" on Encyclopedia.com"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"The Evolution of Motorcycle Style\" on GQ.com"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b7/Petrebels-AR12trGJyjA-unsplash.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20210919183828","caption":"Petrebels-AR12trGJyjA-unsplash","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Petrebels-AR12trGJyjA-unsplash.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0100-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/80/Alex-iby-_ZagmOPlPCE-unsplash.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20210919183817","caption":"Biker · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Alex-iby-_ZagmOPlPCE-unsplash.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0100-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}